nt Project Faculty and Staff Contacts Program Descriptions Counselor Education About Department of Counselor Education Mission Policy on Student Recruitment, Retention, and Development Accreditation, Licensure and Credentialing Program Outcomes Report Faculty and Staff Profiles Contact Us and FAQ Graduate Programs Clinical Mental Health Counseling, M.A. Couple and Family Counseling M.A. Rehabilitation Counseling, M.A. School Counseling, M.A. Master's Programs Application Process Non-Degree Counseling Certificate and Endorsement Programs Graduate Certificate in Couple and Family Counseling Graduate Certificate in Rehabilitation Counseling Non-Degree School Counselor Endorsement Non-Degree Programs Application Process Current and Prospective Student Resources Counselor Education Student Association (CESA) Course Descriptions Information Sessions for Prospective Students Permission to Take Courses in Counselor Education as a Non-Degree Seeking Student Counseling and Wellness Clinic News and Events Program Descriptions Health Sciences, Physical Education, Educational Foundations and Urban Community Studies HSPE/EDFN/UCS/LEI Request Info HSPE/EDFN/UCS/LEI Faculty and Staff Community and Teacher Leaders Admission Requirements Course Sequence News and Events Teacher Union Partnerships Why Choose NEIU's MACTL? Leadership, Equity and Inquiry, Ed.D. Urban Community Studies Health & Physical Education (H&PE) Student Organization Literacy, Leadership, Development, and Special Education B.A. in Human Resource Development Advising Course Requirements Declaring a Major or Minor HRD Internship Internship Proposal Students' Internship Concerns HRD Program Faculty HRD Scholarship Contact Special Education Undergraduate Minor in Human Resource Development Literacy Center M.A. in Higher Education Degree Requirements ENLACE ENLACE Program Application Higher Education Faculty William Itkin Children's Center for Disabilities Application for William Itkin Children's Service Center M.A. in Human Resource Development Admissions Requirements Deadlines Degree Requirements HRD-Related Organizations, Journals & Books Master's Degree Overview Tips for Succeeding at the Comprehensive Exam M.A. in School Leadership Admission Requirements Contact Us Degree Requirements FAQ News & Announcements Partnerships School Leadership Program Faculty Master of Arts in Literacy Education Professional Connections Program Descriptions Department Support Staff Reading Teacher Endorsement (Pre-K to 12) Success of Our Candidates Connect With Us Employment Opportunities Employment Opportunities Thank you for your interest in the Daniel L. Goodwin College of Education. Below you will find current employment opportunities in the College. Faculty, Instructors and Clinical Supervision Positions Clinical Experience Coordinator (Nursing) University Supervisor for Clinical Experiences and Student Teaching Experiences About Northeastern Illinois University Northeastern Illinois University’s Main Campus is located on 67 acres in a residential area on the Northwest Side of Chicago. The University has three additional locations in the metropolitan area: the Jacob H. Carruthers Center for Inner City Studies, El Centro, the Center for College Access and Success and the University Center of Lake County consortium campus in suburban Lake County, north of Chicago. Recognized as one of the most diverse universities in the Midwest, Northeastern offers more than 40 undergraduate degree and certificate programs and more than 50 graduate degree, certificate, licensure and endorsement programs. APPLY Please see the individual position listings above for other required materials and the application deadline.  Applications will not be considered if information is incomplete or submitted after deadlines. Questions about the application process can be directed to the search committee chair identified in the listing. Northeastern offers a rewarding work environment. Information about employment benefits and other resources at: Northeastern Illinois University Office of Human Resources Bernard Office Building 5555 North Bernard Street Chicago, Illinois 60625 The Office of Human Resources is open Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Questions? Call (773) 442-5200. Please note that a criminal background check and other documentation will be required during the onboarding process to NEIU. Thank you for your interest in our faculty and instructor positions. For more job opportunities, visit our Working Here website. Northeastern Illinois University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and invites applications from Women, Minorities, Veterans and Persons with Disabilities, as well as other qualified individuals. Northeastern Illinois University positions are contingent upon the University’s receipt of its State of Illinois appropriation. Our Mission is You Request Information Plan a Visit Apply Now Footer Menu 1 Footer Menu 1 Online Learning Academic Calendar NEIUPort Maps & Directions Housing Events Employment Directory Community Library Main Campus 5500 North St. Louis Avenue Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 583-4050 Carruthers Center 700 East Oakwood Blvd. Chicago, IL 60625 (773) 268-7500 El Centro 3390 North Avondale Ave. Chicago, IL 60618 (773) 442-4080 University Center 1200 University Center Drive, Room 220B Grayslake, IL 60030 (847) 665-4000 Footer bottom Footer bottom Take a Virtual Tour Give to NEIU © 2022 Northeastern Illinois University | Legal | Login Also of Interest Community Engagement Initiatives Campus GCOE Scholarships in Illinois Faculty Profiles ↑"
